  "body": "Lathe cross-drill measures about the work offset's spindle (#67).\n\n**What was wrong**: cross_drill measured every standoff about world Z through world (0,0) - bar radius, station side, hop and clearance radii, the inter-station clearance rule - while the post programs about world Z through the work-offset origin. On an r10 bar at (10,4) under a moved G54 (radii read from G54):\n\n| Rapid point | Before | After (= bar on the origin) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Start | 15.770 | 15.000 |\n| Hop between stations | 26.444 / 32.444 / 46.444 | 21.213 |\n| Final clearance | 35.770 | 15.000 |\n\nAlso: on a mill-turn the #62 spindle law didn't cover cross drilling (a bar 10.770 mm off an unmoved G54 drilled silently); on a plain lathe a part the axis fit can't read as turned drilled anyway.\n\n**What changed**\n- New `crates/app/src/operation/cross_spindle.rs`: shifts holes into the spindle frame by the `wcs_context` origin, measures `stock_r` about that line, runs the drilling kernel unchanged, shifts back; on-origin parts skip the shift (bit-identical). `lathe_reads` refuses by name a part the fit can't read as turned on a plain lathe.\n- `job.rs`: the work-offset origin is read once in `collect_job` (`GenJob::wcs_origin`); the spindle law checks against the same origin.\n- `spindle_law::turns` also covers a mill-turn Drill with cross holes - refused by name at generation and posting; moving G54 stales the op.\n- A mill-turn still drills square/hex bars (normal cross-drill stock), clearance now about the posted spindle (RECOMMENDED.md #67).\n\n**Pinned by** `drilling_cross_spindle::{a_cross_drill_off_the_world_origin_under_a_moved_g54_drills_the_on_origin_chain, a_cross_drill_on_a_bar_off_an_unmoved_work_offset_is_refused_by_name, a_lathe_cross_drill_on_a_part_that_reads_as_no_revolve_is_refused_by_name}` (all fail on main). Goldens unchanged.\n\n**Gates**: quick gate green (app 334 s, ui 337 s); the agent ran drilling_axial, drilling_cross, lathe_spindle_law, lathe_spindle_fit, lathe_post(_refusals), lathe_field_sim, posting, conformance, golden_cl, all turning suites, clippy -D warnings - green.\n\n**Follow-up**: #77 (standoff from the finished part, not the raw stock).\n\nChangelog: fix(app): cross drill measures its clearance and standoffs about the work offset's spindle, refuses a mill-turn bar off its work offset, and refuses on a lathe a part that can't be read as turned\n\nFixes #67\n",
